msgid "exploration.delay.title"
msgstr "One accepted sample later"

msgid "exploration.delay.description"
msgstr "Whenever ACCEPT=1, receive the four-bit DATA and update OUT to the previously accepted value. OUT starts at 0. Accepting 3, 7, 2 produces 0, 3, 7. ACCEPT=0 receives nothing and holds the output."

msgid "exploration.delay.spec"
msgstr "ACCEPT is one-bit control; DATA and OUT are four-bit values (0–15). Each test step has one state-commit boundary; all [[register|registers]] sample the values from before that boundary. Build freely with your [[register|registers]]. Tests include consecutive accepts, repeats, pauses and resumption."

msgid "exploration.delay.hint.1"
msgstr "A wire carries the current value. Where does the previous sample survive when a new one arrives? Which states must hold when acceptance pauses?"

msgid "exploration.delay.hint.2"
msgstr "This partial board stores the latest accepted sample. The output must retain its value from before the update. All registers commit together in the same step."

msgid "exploration.delay.hint.3"
msgstr "Full reference: chain two Register4 components. DATA feeds the first; its Q feeds the second D. ACCEPT feeds both LOAD inputs. The second Q is OUT."

msgid "exploration.delay.summary"
msgstr "You stored current and previous data separately. Pauses, repeated values and consecutive accepts obey the same commit rule."

msgid "experience.next.hardware_foundations.delay"
msgstr "Optional exploration: pause for several steps and resume. This branch does not gate the original RAM route."

msgid "exploration.delay.monitor"
msgstr "Previous accepted sample · OUT = %s"

