msgid "overlap.arrival.title"
msgstr "Issued is not arrived"

msgid "overlap.arrival.goal"
msgstr "Do independent work and process batch 0 within 10 cycles."

msgid "overlap.arrival.body"
msgstr "Repair the small machine. fetch returns immediately, but the data still takes 6 cycles to arrive. The starting program consumes it immediately.\n\nYou also have 4 cycles of work independent of that data. Find a useful place for it, then consume data that has arrived.\n\nInspect the failed line and timeline: request, arrival and completion are distinct moments."

msgid "overlap.buffers.title"
msgstr "Two buffers take turns"

msgid "overlap.buffers.goal"
msgstr "Place and connect storage; process four batches in order, 40 → 28 cycles."

msgid "overlap.buffers.body"
msgstr "Each transfer takes 6 cycles and each computation takes 4. With one buffer, transfer often waits for compute to finish.\n\nThe interior starts empty. Place up to two buffers and connect data, ready and free. The starting program is serial and editable.\n\nNames A and B appear on your components. Program names must match your actual parts."

msgid "overlap.backpressure.title"
msgstr "Slow down without losing data"

msgid "overlap.backpressure.goal"
msgstr "Pass two variable-speed workloads with one program; no overwrites or duplicates."

msgid "overlap.backpressure.body"
msgstr "Two buffers are present, but the schedule uses a fixed tick 4 before reuse. Compute duration now varies.\n\nInspect which buffer is still in use. Coordinate with actual ready, free and compute-idle state so one program handles both public timing patterns.\n\nHolding back a producer to protect unconsumed data is backpressure, not dropping data."

msgid "overlap.prefetch.title"
msgstr "A little earlier"

msgid "overlap.prefetch.goal"
msgstr "Schedule prefetches to reduce the same four batches from 40 to 28 cycles."

msgid "overlap.prefetch.body"
msgstr "A one-line Cache fills and replaces entries automatically. A missing read waits; prefetch can start the transfer earlier.\n\nEdit the schedule so the transfer engine does useful work while compute is busy. Data must still arrive before use.\n\nYou cannot set Cache contents or slots. It differs from the explicit buffers in the other branch."

msgid "overlap.distance.title"
msgstr "Earlier is not always better"

msgid "overlap.distance.goal"
msgstr "Repair over-eager prefetch; keep correct results within 30 cycles."

msgid "overlap.distance.body"
msgstr "The starting schedule requests everything early. Yet Cache has only one line and the request queue holds only two items, including the active transfer.\n\nInspect evictions, repeated transfers and queuing. Which transfer displaces data before it is used?\n\nChange timing rather than setting cache contents. The one-line budget is fixed; costs come from actual transfers and waits."

msgid "overlap.synthesis.title"
msgstr "Keep compute moving"

msgid "overlap.synthesis.goal"
msgstr "Use a two-unit budget and one design for standard and bandwidth-bound tasks."

msgid "overlap.synthesis.body"
msgstr "Choose buffers or Cache and build the interior and schedule. Both routes can succeed; you need not use every tool.\n\nProcess each batch exactly once in order, then check both public workloads. In the second, transfers are slow and compute is fast. Would extra storage make the transfer engine faster?\n\nExplain and improve the bottleneck rather than forcing wait time to zero."

