msgid "system.level.read_once.title"
msgstr "One read is enough"

msgid "system.level.read_once.description"
msgstr "If a number must be added twice, must memory send it twice?\n\nHardware is fixed. The starter is correct but requests the same input twice each iteration. Keep the result correct and reuse the value already fetched."

msgid "system.level.read_once.objective"
msgstr "Goal: OUTPUT[0] is twice the input sum, keeping the low 8 bits (wrap after 255).\n\nEvery dataset must be correct with at most N+1 memory requests: N reads + one final write. At N=16 the starter uses 33 requests; the goal is at most 17.\n\nvalue = load(INPUT[i]) stores data in a variable. Later acc += value uses it without another request. Apply your edited program before official testing. Equivalent programs are accepted.\n\n[[load|LOAD]]"

msgid "system.completion.summary.read_once"
msgstr "You reduced real memory requests without upgrading hardware. Once data arrives, ask whether it can be used again."

msgid "system.level.two_orders.title"
msgstr "One budget, two orders"

msgid "system.level.two_orders.description"
msgstr "Two clients bring different workloads with the same budget. Choose CPU, RAM and Bus separately for each order.\n\nCompute: read one value, perform 32 additions, then write it.\nMove: copy every input item without arithmetic.\n\nSwitch orders at the top of Parts. Each order retains its own configuration; one shared machine is not required."

msgid "system.level.two_orders.objective"
msgstr "Budget ≤24 for each order.\nCompute: every case ≤66 cycles.\nMove: every case ≤320 cycles.\n\nPrograms are fixed; change the parts. Inspect the workload, then check where time goes in the actual Trace. Complete both orders to finish this optional branch.\n\nAll top-tier parts cost 39, above budget. Multiple configurations qualify; there is no single required answer.\n\n[[hardware_cost|Hardware Cost]]"

msgid "system.completion.summary.two_orders"
msgstr "You spent each budget where it mattered. The fastest part is not always the most useful purchase; the workload determines the tradeoff."

msgid "system.orders.compute"
msgstr "Order A · Compute · ≤66 cycles"

msgid "system.orders.move"
msgstr "Order B · Move · ≤320 cycles"

